<td>Around 100–800 units per cycle</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<h2>Pyramid packaging supply and finishes for growing brands</h2>
<p>Finishing choices give pyramid packaging the right surface and strength for everything from sweet treats to skincare minis and keepsakes. We at Shop Cardboard Boxes supply Cardboard Pyramid Boxes at wholesale prices with coating options such as Gloss, Matte, and Spot UV to support different looks and handling needs. Free design and shipping support help you move from early ideas to final print art without unwanted delays, while custom sizes and styles allow the shape to suit single premium items or small grouped sets. Fast turnaround times, high-quality material, and reliable printing options keep both small and large orders flowing in line with launch calendars.</p>
<p>Material selection shapes how the pack behaves in real settings. White boards provide a clean base for sharp colours and fine lines, while natural kraft boards give a warmer, grounded tone that works well with simple darker inks. Heavier boards support stacked displays and longer journeys through courier networks, whereas lighter boards suit events, sampling campaigns, or short-run promotions that stay close to home. Matching finishes across diy-inspired projects and larger commercial runs keeps the brand feeling familiar no matter who is doing the final assembly.</p>
<h3>Choosing materials and surfaces for each pyramid range</h3>
<p>Gloss coatings bring extra clarity and brightness to bold artwork, which suits confectionery, festive gifts, and lively cosmetic lines that need energy at first glance. Matte coatings offer a softer, low-glare surface that helps detailed text and subtle gradients stay legible under strong lighting in stores or at events. Spot UV can be used to highlight logos, icons, or pattern elements with a gentle shine while leaving most of the surface calmer, giving depth without overwhelming the design.</p>
<p>Board weight deserves as much thought as artwork. Heavier grades carry the load for stacked arrangements in windows or at the back of deep shelves. Lighter options make sense when boxes will be assembled on-site at markets, workshops, or seasonal stalls, where quick folding and easy transport matter more than long-term stacking. Across all these choices, the goal is steady behaviour from the box so packers, merchandisers, and customers all feel that the shape supports their part of the journey.</p>
<p><strong>Material and finish options to consider</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Gloss-coated white board for bright, colourful product stories</li>
<li>Matte-coated white board for calm, low-reflection surfaces</li>
<li>Spot UV on selected areas to draw attention to key brand details</li>
<li>Natural kraft materials for earthier, more relaxed presentations</li>
<li>Heavy-duty board grades for larger pyramids and stacked displays</li>
<li>Lightweight board styles for quick assembly at events and pop-ups</li>
<li>Colour-managed printing so tones stay consistent across seasons</li>
<li>Matching inner and outer finishes when unboxing is part of the experience</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Checklist for finalising pyramid box specifications</strong></p>
<ol>
<li>Confirm where your pyramids will appear, from shelves and counters to mailers.</li>
<li>Choose board weight based on stacking needs and shipping distances.</li>
<li>Pick a primary coating type that suits your lighting and brand style.</li>
<li>Decide whether small areas of Spot UV will help key elements stand out.</li>
<li>Align material choices with other packaging in your range for a unified feel.</li>
<li>Review artwork proofs at full size to check line sharpness and text legibility.</li>
<li>Approve colour samples under the lighting conditions where boxes will be seen.</li>
<li>Lock in production timelines so deliveries match your planned launch or restock dates.</li>
</ol>
